      "writtenOn": "2019-11-04T17:45:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am inclined to introduce CHARGE_PORT_MAX_COUNT and define CHARGE_PORT_MAX_COUNT \u0026 CHARGE_PORT_COUNT as follows:\n#define CHARGE_PORT_MAX_COUNT CONFIG_USB_PD_PORT_MAX_COUNT + CONFIG_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT_COUNT\n#define CHARGE_PORT_COUNT board_get_usb_pd_port_count() + CONFIG_DEDICATED_CHARGE_PORT_COUNT\nThat will help to ensure that there are no gaps in the available_charge_array.\n\nAlso I see quite a lot of places where CHARGE_PORT_COUNT is used - like registration_time, charge_ceil, dual_role_capability etc. where there will be holes which is not accounted for.\n\nThis will make it cleaner. Thoughts??",
